---
{
  title: "resolve_path"
}
---
### NAME

    resolve_path() - Resolves a path against a base directory into a
    canonical absolute mudlib path.

### SYNOPSIS

    string resolve_path( string base_dir, string path );

### DESCRIPTION

    Resolves a path against a base directory into a canonical absolute
    mudlib path.

    Relative paths resolve against base_dir; absolute paths (a leading '/')
    ignore it. '.' and '..' components are collapsed, with '..' clamped at
    the root, and a trailing '.' or '..' component leaves a trailing slash.
    Special forms: here -> the source file of the caller's current
    environment ~ -> the caller's home directory ~/rest -> the caller's home
    directory, then rest ~name -> that user's home directory ~name/rest ->
    that user's home directory, then rest

### PARAMETERS

    base_dir  (string)
              Directory that relative paths resolve against.

    path      (string)
              The path to resolve.

### RETURN VALUES

    (string) The resolved absolute path.
